---
import { cardCls, crumbCls } from '../lib/ui';
// One outside model (#/leaderboard/competitor/<model>), or a Thorp version (#/leaderboard/thorp/<ship_key>, its ship's
// sailings averaged, leaderboard.thorp_entry): a 2-4B competitor or a reference ladder model, as read on Thorp's
// tests (data/compare/chain-grades.json, /api/competitor). Its chaining result and the logic deck, its cards (the stars
// that do the trick, read by Thorp's cards evaluator), and every rung of the four chains: those are Thorp's internal
// measures, shown here because this page describes the competitor, not Thorp. UI.md, "Leaderboard".
---
<div class="section" id="competitor">
  <h1><a class={crumbCls('back')} href="#/leaderboard">← leaderboard</a> <span id="cptitle"></span> <span id="cppills"></span></h1>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><div class="rungover" id="cpover"></div></section>

  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
    <h2>Chaining two facts <span class="note">the four chaining tests (each its lift and share of pairs right, ✓ performed: lift 0.1 and two in three right), and the logic deck, the proof that a pass is chaining: invented words and counterfactual premises, each item asked with both premises, with one, swapped and padded, and at one, two and three hops</span></h2>
    <div class="cpsum" id="cpsum"></div>
    <div class="scroll"><table id="cptests" data-nosort><thead><tr><th>test</th><th>chain</th><th>lift</th><th>share right</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    <div class="row cplogic">
      <div><div class="k">The logic deck: each way of asking <span class="s">mean lift; the gain is both premises less the better single one</span></div><div class="chart" id="cpvariants"></div></div>
      <div><div class="k">By kind of relation <span class="s">the chaining gain on each</span></div><div class="chart" id="cprelations"></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
    <h2>Its hand <span class="note">the stars that do the trick, as playing cards: a card lit inside the model (at its mark by one head, or shared by two) is in its hand; one it hasn't lit is still in the deck, set aside face down with how close it came; "unreadable" where its attention can't be read through MLX-LM. Every model, outside or Thorp, is read by the same reader with its own tokeniser (previous-word and Nevermore on Goldsmith's essays, cards.copying_cards)</span></h2>
    <div id="cpcards"></div>
  </section>

  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="cpknockout" hidden>
    <h2>The knockout <span class="note">each card's 8 strongest heads silenced (their outputs zeroed on every pass) and the logic deck read again, beside three random draws of 8 heads from no card: a card is necessary when silencing it costs at least 0.1 of the cause gain (the comparator: the order gain) and more than twice the largest random drop (DECISIONS.md, "The knockout, pre-registered")</span></h2>
    <div id="cpknock"></div>
  </section>

  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
    <h2>Every rung <span class="note">the four discovery chains, keel to the 50m (two facts chained); these are Thorp's internal measures, shown because this page describes the competitor. Each cell its lift and share right, ✓ performed</span></h2>
    <div class="scroll"><table id="cprungs" data-nosort><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
  </section>
</div>
